      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1i6svrc'
    'male|a||The hospital trap looks different drawn as arrows: coverage on the left, health on the right, and the arrow between them is the effect we want.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Sickness drives health too. Nobody measures it well, but in this illustration the lottery alone decides coverage, so no arrow joins those two.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1whbt9r'
    'male|a||Admission to hospital has two causes: coverage makes a bed easier to get, and sickness makes one necessary.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:reogk5'
    male|a||Two arrowheads meet at admission, and a node where arrows collide is called a collider.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:zyz6jr'
    'male|a||Left alone, a collider blocks the path through it: coverage and sickness both pour into admission, and nothing flows back out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9zeewo'
    male|a||Comparing only the admitted draws a box round the collider, and the box opens the path.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:juuyr5'
    male|a||Inside the hospital, an insured patient needed less sickness to get a bed, so coverage now tells you about sickness, and sickness about health.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1y1kvir'
    'male|a||That is where the false five points come from: coverage added fifty healthier admissions per thousand, and the gap at health reads five.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:oir77h'
    male|a||So the leak should grow and shrink with the arrow into admission.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jt0nmi'
    male|a||Watch the gap at health shrink to nothing as the arrow into admission weakens, and grow as it strengthens.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ersgsb'
    'male|a||With no extra admissions, the gap at health falls to zero: no arrow into the collider, no leak.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||At a hundred and fifty extra beds, it climbs to ten.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:65mjof'
    male|a||Statisticians met this trap long before economists. In 1946 Joseph Berkson showed that hospital patients can link two diseases that are unrelated outside.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ephz24'
    male|a||Its best-known case in medicine is the birth-weight paradox, and it sits on the same four nodes.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jdqlip'
    male|a||In American births from 1991, babies of smokers were more often born small, and more often died in their first year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:koivbl'
    'male|a||Yet among the babies born small, those of smokers died less often, by about a fifth: a rate ratio of 0.79.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9mij1u'
    'male|a||The arrows say why: a small baby whose mother did not smoke is more often small for a worse reason, such as a birth defect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8p09yx'
    male|a||In 2006 Hernández-Díaz, Schisterman and Hernán showed that collider bias can explain it, with no protective effect of smoking needed.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1t04l5c'
    male|a||Back to Oregon, with a new choice. Oregon's researchers wanted the effect of winning the lottery. Which of these could they safely control for?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12ae9ty'
    'male|a||Household size: it was fixed before the draw, so winning cannot move it. Oregon''s own analysis controlled for it, because a whole household''s chances depended on it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||The rule, in arrows: never put a box round a collider on a path between treatment and outcome, or round anything the treatment itself moves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||So are arrows and potential outcomes two theories of cause, or two notations for the same one?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||On one side, Judea Pearl argues that a graph like this one makes every assumption visible: each missing arrow is a claim you can see, and safe controls follow by rule.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12fvk5s'
    male|a||On the other, Guido Imbens, writing for economists in 2020, replies that the designs economists use rest on assumptions a graph cannot draw.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6zbf5p'
    'male|a||Formally, the two are closer than the quarrel sounds: what a graph claims can be rewritten as claims about potential outcomes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12s1cun'
    'male|a||So the question is practical, and what would settle it is a record, not a theorem: which habit leaves working researchers making fewer mistakes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:174pxux'
    'male|a||So test both sides on this graph: the lottery, Z, used to measure what coverage does, because winning raises the chance of being covered.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1se8636'
    male|a||Coverage moves health, and sickness moves both, because in reality people choose whether to enrol. Only the lottery is clear of sickness.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:yzbacv'
    male|a||In Oregon, winning raised coverage by only about a quarter, so the lottery moved a minority.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:x2mxbv'
    male|a||To turn the lottery's effect into coverage's effect, winning must never push anyone away from coverage.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10sopxv'
    male|a||Yet a world with such people, who would enrol only if they lost, draws exactly the same arrow.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xrs0gl'
    'male|a||In potential outcomes the assumption takes one line: each person''s coverage if they win is at least their coverage if they lose.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kh4wqc'
    male|a||And what the lottery then measures is the average effect for the compliers, the people it moved. The graph has no symbol for them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:98fxyr'
    male|a||Pearl answers that such a restriction lives in the equations behind the graph, even where no arrow shows it, and that it is the same condition in both notations.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jiprof'
    male|a||One last check. Which assumption about Oregon's lottery can the graph's arrows not show?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xspc51'
    'male|a||The last one: an arrow from the lottery to coverage says that winning matters, not which way it pushes for each person. The other two are missing arrows, which a graph shows well.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||So can a careful control create bias? Yes, when the treatment itself moves it: admission reopened the gap the lottery had closed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||The arrows find such traps at a glance, so draw them before choosing what to control for.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:118vu87'
